  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_breeze",
      "name": {
        "en": "Breeze's Badge",
        "zh": "微风证章",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "original",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Breeze has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for healing several teammates in a short period of time. \nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution: \nThis operator shall be appointed a Medic Operator during field operations to exercise Multi-target Medic responsibilities. \nIn witness whereof, \nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员微风擅长在短时间内为数位干员提供治疗\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为医疗干员，行使群愈师职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_breeze",
      "name": {
        "en": "Surgical Instrument Kit",
        "zh": "外科医疗套组",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_breeze",
      "description": {
        "en": "Grace, my dear. \nYou haven't contacted us since you left home. \nAt first we thought you were still angry because of the argument, but later, we learned what happened to you. \nBefore, we didn't even have a way to celebrate your birthday. But now, we know the address of your workplace. \nHappy birthday, my dear Grace. \nInside this package is my present to you, a toolbag. \nWhen I was young, I always wanted to venture far away, so I asked a famous craftsman in Londinium to make this toolbag. It's very durable, and can hold a lot of things. \nBut after that, I returned to the life that my parents planned out for me, so I never had a chance to use it. \nEven though this world has many ways of stopping a person in her tracks, I believe that you can go further than me. \nYour father is very disappointed in himself. He wants to go to Rhodes Island to look for you, but doesn't know how to face you, nor does he know how to deal with what would come next. If you ever see him, I hope you two can sit down and talk things through. \nMy daughter, no matter what happens, I will always support your decisions and your dreams. \nIf Henry disagrees with you, then I'll talk him into it. \nOne last thing: Your father found someone to make a whole bunch of those sweets you used to love as a kid, even though he was also the one who forbade you from having them... If they show up in the mail, don't eat them all at once! \n \n––Beatrix Arizona \n \n \nGrace, I made a trip to Rhodes Island. Your coworker said you were out in the field, in some dangerous place no less. Something about being a battlefield medic for Rhodes Island. \nThe way I understand things is, Rhodes Island might be one of the best places in this world, but if you stay here, you should behave like a patient rather than running amok like you are now. \nWe can afford the cost of your treatment, but we can't afford to lose you a second time. \nI've brought you some food and supplies. Some of it's perishable, so don't forget to eat it. \nIf you ever need anything, just let me know. \nBeatrix wants me to sit down and have a good talk with you, so I'll come back next month. \nAlso, your mother wants to hear back from you more often. \nThe desk drawer in your dorm was broken, so I repaired it. Try not to stuff too many things in there. \n\n––Henry Arizona",
        "zh": "格蕾丝，我的宝贝。\n自你离家到现在，你都没有联系过我们。\n起初我们以为是你还在为那次争吵生气，后来，我们才知道在你身上发生的事。\n之前我们没法为你过生日，但现在，我们知道了你工作的地址。\n生日快乐，我的格蕾丝。\n这份包裹里是我送给你的生日礼物，一个工具包。\n我年轻时，一直很想去远方冒险，就找伦蒂尼姆有名的皮匠制作了这个工具包。它可以装很多东西，而且非常耐用。\n之后，我回归了父母为我规划好的生活，从来没有机会真正使用它。\n纵使这片大地上有许多因素会使人止步，但我相信，你可以比我走得更远。\n你的爸爸非常自责，他想去罗德岛找你，但又不知道该怎么面对你，也不知道如何面对之后的事情。如果你见到他，你们最好静下心来好好谈谈。\n我的女儿，无论如何，我都支持你的选择，支持你的理想。\n亨利如果不同意，我会帮你一起说服他。\n注：你爸好像找人给你做了很多你小时候爱吃的甜食，明明当时不允许你吃的也是他……如果收到那些甜食，不要一次吃太多！\n\n——碧娅特丽丝·亚利桑那\n\n\n格蕾丝，我去了罗德岛一趟，你的同事说你正在出外勤，还去了特别危险的地方，说什么为罗德岛提供战场医疗救护服务。\n根据我的了解，罗德岛可能确实是这片大地上数一数二的，但你留在这边，理应作为一个病人接受治疗，而不是像现在这样到处乱跑。\n我们能负担治疗所需的费用，但我不能接受再一次失去你。\n我带了一些吃和用的过来，有一些保质期很短，别忘了吃。\n你需要什么，就跟我说。\n碧娅特丽丝要我和你面对面好好谈谈，所以下个月我会再来一次。\n还有，记得多给你老妈写信。\n你宿舍的书桌抽屉坏了，我已帮你修好。别往抽屉里塞太多东西。\n\n——亨利·亚利桑那",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
